More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (851–860)
851. Improper Validation of API Version Parameters
API Version Manipulation
Attackers change API version numbers to access deprecated or insecure endpoints.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
852. Insecure Handling of Notification Delivery Systems
Notification System Manipulation
Attackers exploit notification systems to send unauthorized alerts or hide important notifications.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
853. Improper Validation of Image Processing APIs
Image Processing API Vulnerability
Image manipulation APIs process untrusted input, allowing code execution or system compromise.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
854. Insecure Handling of Temporary File Storage
Temporary File Exposure
Temporary files stored on servers expose sensitive data to unauthorized users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
855. Improper Validation of User Session Revocation
Session Revocation Failure
User sessions remain active even after logout or password changes.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
856. Insecure Handling of Chat Message APIs
Chat API Authorization Bypass
Attackers read or send messages belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
857. Improper Validation of User Avatar Uploads
Avatar Upload Vulnerability
Malicious files uploaded as avatars execute scripts or expose server files.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
858. Insecure Handling of Report Generation Services
Report Generation Data Exposure
Report generation APIs expose sensitive data or internal system information.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
859. Improper Validation of API Filtering Rules
API Filter Manipulation
Attackers modify filtering rules to reveal hidden or restricted records.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
860. Insecure Handling of Background Job Queues
Background Job Queue Exposure
Attackers manipulate queued background jobs to execute unauthorized actions.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
